00:28:33.740 --> 00:28:37.500
Because then it would have just been like kind of a white button-down shirt and pants.
因为那样的话，看起来就只是一件普通的白衬衫和裤子了。

637
00:28:37.640 --> 00:28:38.700
I don't think it would have mattered.
我觉得那应该没什么影响。

638
00:28:38.980 --> 00:28:40.600
It's a weird white shirt, right?
那是一件奇怪的白衬衫，对吧？

639
00:28:40.700 --> 00:28:42.360
It does have the tuxedo collar.
它确实有燕尾服的领子。

640
00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:43.120
Yeah.
没错。

641
00:28:43.400 --> 00:28:44.620
But it would have helped.
但那样做会有帮助的。

642
00:28:45.180 --> 00:28:46.860
It would have maybe helped a little.
或许能有一点帮助。

643
00:28:47.020 --> 00:28:48.900
I'm going to say good point, guys.
我要说，你们说得很有道理。

644
00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:56.800
This whole dynamic of Jim and Charles getting off on the wrong foot, this is going to extend,
吉姆和查尔斯这种开局不利的互动关系，会一直持续下去，

645
00:28:56.980 --> 00:28:59.560
you know, because Idris is going to be on for five more episodes.
你知道，因为伊德里斯还要再演五集。

646
00:28:59.560 --> 00:29:04.000
And this is going to extend through this whole storyline with him.
这种关系会贯穿他整个故事线。

647
00:29:04.260 --> 00:29:09.400
And this was a dynamic Gene and Lee told me that the writers really wanted to examine.
吉恩和李告诉我，编剧们非常想探讨这种互动关系。

648
00:29:09.620 --> 00:29:12.860
They loved this idea that someone was going to put Jim back on his heels.
他们很喜欢这个点子，就是有人能让吉姆感到措手不及。

649
00:29:13.140 --> 00:29:17.120
That there was a character that was immune to Jim's charm and wit.
有一个角色对吉姆的魅力和机智完全免疫。

650
00:29:17.660 --> 00:29:23.360
And they thought it would be very, very funny to see Jim be so disarmed.
他们觉得看吉姆被搞得如此不知所措会非常、非常有趣。

651
00:29:24.260 --> 00:29:25.220
It was.
确实如此。

652
00:29:25.420 --> 00:29:26.900
I couldn't get enough of it.
我怎么看都看不够。

653
00:29:26.980 --> 00:29:27.620
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

654
00:29:27.620 --> 00:29:33.180
I loved John, everything about John, having to play this piece of his character.
我喜欢约翰，喜欢关于约翰的一切，喜欢饰演他这个角色的一部分。

655
00:29:33.460 --> 00:29:35.060
And you know John had so much fun.
而且你知道，约翰当时玩得很开心。

656
00:29:35.220 --> 00:29:38.600
That was just always really cool when you got to examine another side of your character.
当你能审视角色性格的另一面时，那感觉总是非常棒。

657
00:29:38.880 --> 00:29:40.260
I loved that, too.
我也很喜欢那样。

658
00:29:40.360 --> 00:29:45.400
I always loved when there would be little shifts like when Pam and Dwight were friends.
我一直很喜欢那些小小的转变，比如帕姆和德怀特成为朋友的时候。

659
00:29:45.620 --> 00:29:45.880
Yeah.
是啊。

660
00:29:46.280 --> 00:29:46.660
You know?
你懂吗？

661
00:29:46.820 --> 00:29:47.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

662
00:29:47.240 --> 00:29:48.720
I love suspicious bitch.
我喜欢那个多疑的贱人。

663
00:29:49.220 --> 00:29:49.900
You know?
你懂吗？

664
00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:50.920
So.
所以。

665
00:29:51.900 --> 00:29:58.340
But now, one of my favorite elements of our show is when Michael has to introduce a new
但现在，我们剧里我最喜欢的元素之一，就是迈克尔不得不向办公室里的任何人介绍

666
00:29:58.340 --> 00:30:00.140
person to anyone in the office.
一个新人的时候。

667
00:30:00.460 --> 00:30:02.260
He gets so personal.
他总是表现得非常私人化。

668
00:30:02.540 --> 00:30:05.060
He has done this time and time again.
他一次又一次地这样做。

669
00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:09.340
He brings over the accounting department and then tells all of our dating history.
他把会计部的人叫过来，然后把我们所有的约会史都抖出来。

670
00:30:09.500 --> 00:30:16.320
He tells about Oscar's breakup with Gil and how Angela has had sexual relations with Andy.
他会讲奥斯卡和吉尔的分手，还有安吉拉和安迪有过性关系的事。

671
00:30:16.320 --> 00:30:20.800
And then Idris just interrupts him and is like, you know, Michael, I don't need to know everyone's
然后伊德里斯就会打断他，说，你知道吗，迈克尔，我不需要知道每个人的

672
00:30:20.800 --> 00:30:21.580
sexual history.
性生活史。

673
00:30:22.340 --> 00:30:25.220
And he's like, good, because we're getting to Kevin and he's got nada.
而他会说，很好，因为我们要讲到凯文了，而他什么都没有。

674
00:30:26.580 --> 00:30:27.620
I just love it.
我真是太喜欢了。

675
00:30:27.780 --> 00:30:28.380
Every time.
每次都是。

676
00:30:29.040 --> 00:30:30.620
Every time I look forward to it.
每次我都很期待。

677
00:30:30.740 --> 00:30:35.400
Like, the writers must have loved having to come up with new ways for Michael to introduce
编剧们一定很喜欢想出各种新花样，让迈克尔去介绍

678
00:30:35.400 --> 00:30:36.360
the same people.
同一批人。

679
00:30:36.860 --> 00:30:40.900
It really reminds me of how children, like, sometimes introduce people.
这真的让我想起小孩子有时介绍人的方式。

680
00:30:41.060 --> 00:30:41.380
Yes.
没错。

681
00:30:41.580 --> 00:30:43.780
Like, my mom has this story of me.
比如，我妈有个关于我的故事。

682
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:48.160
I was probably, like, eight years old and we were at the grocery store checkout and it
我当时大概八岁，我们在杂货店结账，

683
00:30:48.160 --> 00:30:49.980
was me and my mom and my friend.
当时是我、我妈还有我的朋友。

684
00:30:50.480 --> 00:30:53.180
And the woman thought my friend was my mom's daughter.
那个女人以为我朋友是我妈的女儿。

685
00:30:53.380 --> 00:30:55.620
And she was like, oh, she looks just like you.
她说，噢，她长得真像你。

686
00:30:55.760 --> 00:30:57.560
And I said, that's not her daughter.
我说，那不是她女儿。

687
00:30:57.680 --> 00:30:58.180
I'm her daughter.
我是她女儿。

688
00:30:58.280 --> 00:30:59.300
My mom dyes her hair.
我妈染了头发。

689
00:31:00.620 --> 00:31:02.880
And my mom was like, thank you.
我妈当时说，谢谢你。

690
00:31:02.880 --> 00:31:05.920
But that's how Michael introduces people.
但迈克尔介绍人的方式就是那样。

691
00:31:06.160 --> 00:31:06.940
No, it's true.
不，这是真的。

692
00:31:07.160 --> 00:31:08.680
He's like, hmm, how can I introduce this person?
他会想，嗯，我该怎么介绍这个人呢？

693
00:31:08.860 --> 00:31:09.720
You know what?
你知道吗？

694
00:31:09.920 --> 00:31:11.540
They only have eight toes.
他们只有八个脚趾。

695
00:31:12.100 --> 00:31:12.600
What?
什么？

696
00:31:13.420 --> 00:31:14.660
Here's something interesting.
这里有个有趣的事实。

697
00:31:15.740 --> 00:31:19.840
Charles clearly realizes he needs to take over here for a second.
查尔斯显然意识到他需要暂时接管这里。

698
00:31:20.060 --> 00:31:21.140
He's all business.
他一切公事公办。

699
00:31:21.540 --> 00:31:22.220
He is.
确实是。

700
00:31:22.220 --> 00:31:28.860
And he wants everybody to know that Dunder Mifflin is cutting 3% across the board.
他想让每个人都知道邓德·米夫林公司正在全面裁员3%。

701
00:31:29.060 --> 00:31:32.440
They will no longer be matching 401k contributions.
他们将不再提供401k养老金计划的配套缴费。

702
00:31:33.180 --> 00:31:35.620
All overtime has to go through corporate.
所有加班申请都必须经过总公司审批。

703
00:31:36.740 --> 00:31:38.240
And here's the big one.
还有最重要的一点。

704
00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:43.280
They're putting a freeze on discretionary spending, including parties.
他们要冻结可自由支配的开支，包括聚会费用。

705
00:31:43.860 --> 00:31:46.640
Petty cash, supplies, and parties.
备用金、办公用品和聚会费用。

706
00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:48.380
Oh, boy.
天哪。

707
00:31:48.580 --> 00:31:49.080
Oh, boy.
天哪。

708
00:31:49.280 --> 00:31:52.180
And immediately, Michael starts to spiral.
迈克尔立刻就开始失控了。

709
00:31:52.900 --> 00:31:54.960
He's like, okay, Charles, thanks for coming in.
他当时就像是，好的，查尔斯，谢谢你过来。

710
00:31:55.100 --> 00:31:55.380
Thank you.
谢谢你。

711
00:31:55.500 --> 00:31:56.200
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

712
00:31:56.360 --> 00:31:59.960
And Charles is like, no, I'm actually going to stay today.
而查尔斯却说，不，我今天其实要留下来。

713
00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:01.820
And we got some mail about that.
我们收到了一些关于此事的邮件。

714
00:32:01.820 --> 00:32:07.380
People were like, why is David Wallace having Charles Minor babysit Michael all day when just
大家都在问，为什么大卫·华莱士要让查尔斯·迈纳整天盯着迈克尔，明明在

