Well, Charles wants to know what the heck they're doing in there.
好吧，查尔斯想知道他们到底在里面搞什么鬼。

967
00:42:45.530 --> 00:42:47.430
He now has been tipped off by Phyllis.
他现在已经从菲利斯那里得到了风声。

968
00:42:47.510 --> 00:42:48.870
This is a big waste of time.
这简直是在浪费时间。

969
00:42:49.290 --> 00:42:51.230
And he starts to look over Jim's shoulder.
然后他开始越过吉姆的肩膀看过去。

970
00:42:51.630 --> 00:42:54.290
And he's like, what is a two-way petting zoo?
他问，什么是双向爱抚动物园？

971
00:42:54.970 --> 00:42:56.430
And Jim is really embarrassed.
吉姆当时真的很尴尬。

972
00:42:56.430 --> 00:42:59.370
And he says, you pet the animals, they pet you back.
他说，你爱抚动物，动物也爱抚你。

973
00:42:59.510 --> 00:43:00.630
We could not get through that.
我们当时根本没法演下去。

974
00:43:01.190 --> 00:43:03.690
Two-way petting zoo did us in every time.
双向爱抚动物园每次都让我们笑场。

975
00:43:04.150 --> 00:43:05.690
I got a little bit curious.
我当时有点好奇。

976
00:43:06.150 --> 00:43:08.130
You did not look up two-way petting zoo.
你没去查双向爱抚动物园吧。

977
00:43:08.270 --> 00:43:08.710
I did.
我查了。

978
00:43:09.050 --> 00:43:09.530
Oh, no.
噢，不。

979
00:43:09.870 --> 00:43:10.850
Is that at Burning Man?
那是火人节上的吗？

980
00:43:11.010 --> 00:43:13.370
Because I have a friend who was in a petting zoo at Burning Man.
因为我有个朋友曾在火人节上进过爱抚动物园。

981
00:43:13.730 --> 00:43:14.170
What?
什么？

982
00:43:14.750 --> 00:43:15.930
What is that?
那是什么？

983
00:43:16.570 --> 00:43:17.670
What is that?
那是什么？

984
00:43:17.890 --> 00:43:23.670
You know what I did improv with?
你知道我和谁一起做过即兴表演吗？

985
00:43:24.190 --> 00:43:25.450
And I'll never forget.
我永远忘不了。

986
00:43:25.830 --> 00:43:28.230
You know, she's kind of like a free spirit.
你知道，她那种人比较崇尚自由。

987
00:43:28.550 --> 00:43:30.050
And I was at the airport.
当时我在机场。

988
00:43:30.050 --> 00:43:31.010
This is years ago.
那是几年前的事了。

989
00:43:31.010 --> 00:43:33.050
And I see her running through the airport.
我看到她跑过机场。

990
00:43:33.070 --> 00:43:36.810
And it looked like she had like, I don't know, she had like a carry-on.
看起来她好像带了个随身行李。

991
00:43:36.890 --> 00:43:39.450
But you could see sort of like a onesie poking out of it.
但你能看到里面露出一件连体衣之类的东西。

992
00:43:39.970 --> 00:43:40.830
She's running through the airport.
她跑过机场。

993
00:43:40.950 --> 00:43:41.730
I'm like, hi.
我说，嗨。

994
00:43:41.990 --> 00:43:42.630
And she's like, hi.
她说，嗨。

995
00:43:43.010 --> 00:43:44.650
And she's like, so good to see you.
她说，见到你真好。

996
00:43:44.730 --> 00:43:45.370
And I was like, you too.
我说，我也是。

997
00:43:45.470 --> 00:43:46.310
She's like, where are you going?
她说，你要去哪儿？

998
00:43:46.410 --> 00:43:47.730
And I was like, I'm going to see my folks.
我说，我要去看我父母。

999
00:43:47.770 --> 00:43:48.710
I said, what about you?
我说，你呢？

1000
00:43:49.230 --> 00:43:51.270
And she said, oh, I'm going to Burning Man.
她说，哦，我要去火人节。

1001
00:43:51.270 --> 00:43:53.510
I'm in the petting zoo this year.
我今年在宠物动物园工作。

1002
00:43:54.350 --> 00:43:58.370
And so I had to say, what's a petting zoo?
所以我不得不问，什么是宠物动物园？

1003
00:43:58.590 --> 00:44:01.950
And she was like, well, you know, you dress up as animals and let people pet you.
她说，嗯，你知道的，就是打扮成动物，让人们抚摸你。

1004
00:44:03.130 --> 00:44:03.610
Wow.
哇。

1005
00:44:04.010 --> 00:44:04.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1006
00:44:04.810 --> 00:44:05.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1007
00:44:06.350 --> 00:44:09.750
That's what I thought of when you said that.
你这么一说，我脑子里想的也是这个。

1008
00:44:10.190 --> 00:44:12.530
I did not know that.
我之前还真不知道。

1009
00:44:12.970 --> 00:44:17.750
I mean, I found out that there's no such thing as a two-way petting zoo where actual animals
我是说，我发现根本没有那种真正的动物抚摸人类的“双向宠物动物园”，

1010
00:44:17.750 --> 00:44:22.130
pet the humans, but I did not know about this human petting zoo at Burning Man.
但我确实不知道火人节上还有这种人类宠物动物园。

1011
00:44:22.330 --> 00:44:24.270
Did you think animals would pet humans?
你以为会有动物来抚摸人类吗？

1012
00:44:24.850 --> 00:44:25.910
You know what, lady?
我说这位女士，

1013
00:44:26.050 --> 00:44:26.750
I didn't know.
我哪知道啊。

1014
00:44:26.910 --> 00:44:28.530
I admit it was a weird Google.
我承认我当时搜这个词挺奇怪的。

1015
00:44:28.790 --> 00:44:29.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1016
00:44:29.250 --> 00:44:30.710
But I did find this.
但我确实搜到了这个。

1017
00:44:31.030 --> 00:44:31.230
What?
什么？

1018
00:44:32.050 --> 00:44:40.130
Two-way petting zoo is apparently like a euphemism for describing like a really intense,
“双向宠物动物园”显然是一个委婉语，用来形容那种非常激烈、

1019
00:44:41.110 --> 00:44:42.650
passionate sexual encounter.
充满激情的性行为。

1020
00:44:43.350 --> 00:44:49.190
Like you would be like, oh, me and my boyfriend had a real two-way petting zoo last night.
就像你会说，哦，我和我男朋友昨晚进行了一场真正的“双向宠物动物园”活动。

1021
00:44:49.510 --> 00:44:50.350
No, come on.
别闹了。

1022
00:44:50.430 --> 00:44:51.270
Who talks like that?
谁会那样说话？

1023
00:44:51.550 --> 00:44:54.850
But you are giving me flashbacks of like sixth grade sex ed.
但你让我想起了六年级性教育课的阴影。

1024
00:44:55.070 --> 00:44:58.570
We're like, we had a coach teach us sixth grade sex ed.
当时我们有个教练教我们六年级性教育。

1025
00:44:58.650 --> 00:45:00.610
And he was like, sometimes there's heavy petting.
他说，有时候会有“深度抚摸”。

1026
00:45:00.910 --> 00:45:01.350
Sometimes.
有时候。

1027
00:45:01.710 --> 00:45:02.270
We're like, ah!
我们当时就想，啊！

1028
00:45:04.810 --> 00:45:05.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1029
00:45:05.910 --> 00:45:06.650
I don't know.
我不知道。

1030
00:45:06.870 --> 00:45:11.090
Well, we don't know what Jim meant, but we know he's super embarrassed.
好吧，我们不知道吉姆是什么意思，但我们知道他非常尴尬。

1031
00:45:11.430 --> 00:45:12.770
Well, Charles has had enough.
好吧，查尔斯受够了。

1032
00:45:12.770 --> 00:45:16.150
He wants to dissolve the PPC, effective immediately.
他想立即解散派对策划委员会。

1033
00:45:16.710 --> 00:45:19.130
This is where Michael completely flips out.
这就是迈克尔彻底崩溃的地方。

1034
00:45:19.350 --> 00:45:24.370
And there was a deleted scene where he made a defensive argument to keep the PPC.
还有一个被删减的片段，他为了保住派对策划委员会进行了辩护。

1035
00:45:24.810 --> 00:45:26.450
Oh, we need to hear it.
哦，我们得听听。

1036
00:45:27.010 --> 00:45:30.750
The party planning committee is an institution in this institution.
派对策划委员会是这个机构里的一个机构。

1037
00:45:30.790 --> 00:45:37.210
It is something that I incorporated in the mid-90s to celebrate the laser disc release of
这是我在90年代中期为了庆祝《红粉联盟》发行激光影碟而成立的。

1038
00:45:37.210 --> 00:45:38.090
A League of Their Own.
《红粉联盟》。

1039
00:45:38.230 --> 00:45:39.930
It has become a tradition here.
它已经成为了这里的一种传统。

1040
00:45:40.150 --> 00:45:42.490
It is something that is important to all of us.
这对我们所有人来说都很重要。

1041
00:45:42.490 --> 00:45:44.270
What did we do for League of Their Own party?
我们当时为《红粉联盟》派对做了什么？

1042
00:45:44.370 --> 00:45:45.790
A pizza of your own party.
“披萨联盟”派对。

1043
00:45:46.070 --> 00:45:47.110
Make your own pizza.
自己动手做披萨。

1044
00:45:47.310 --> 00:45:48.310
I didn't even work here then.
那时候我甚至还没在这儿工作呢。

1045
00:45:48.490 --> 00:45:49.190
I just shared the stories.
我只是分享了这些故事。

1046
00:45:49.210 --> 00:45:50.150
Okay, thank you, Dwight.
好了，谢谢你，德怀特。

1047
00:45:50.250 --> 00:45:51.990
That should take five minutes of one person's day.
那应该只需要一个人花五分钟时间就能搞定。

1048
00:45:52.150 --> 00:45:52.430
Really?
真的吗？

1049
00:45:52.590 --> 00:45:53.070
Five minutes.
五分钟。

1050
00:45:54.250 --> 00:45:54.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1051
00:45:55.710 --> 00:45:58.670
And then that's where the scene picks up.
然后场景就从那里接上了。

1052
00:45:58.730 --> 00:46:01.670
And he just goes off and he's like, you don't even know how paper is made.
他突然爆发了，他说，你甚至都不知道纸是怎么造出来的。

1053
00:46:01.690 --> 00:46:02.610
It's not like steel.
它又不是钢。

1054
00:46:02.610 --> 00:46:03.830
You don't put it in a furnace.
你不用把它放进熔炉里。

1055
00:46:03.970 --> 00:46:06.330
And he starts like to cry.
然后他开始哭了起来。

1056
00:46:06.330 --> 00:46:09.930
And he shoves over a chair on his way out.
离开的时候他还推倒了一把椅子。

1057
00:46:10.090 --> 00:46:11.370
That was not in the script.
那可不在剧本里。

1058
00:46:11.630 --> 00:46:12.930
He has a whole tantrum.
他大发了一通脾气。

1059
00:46:13.230 --> 00:46:14.390
Ah, I remember.
啊，我想起来了。

1060
00:46:14.890 --> 00:46:18.930
After Michael leaves, Jim is going to attempt to start over with Charles.
迈克尔离开后，吉姆打算和查尔斯重新开始。

1061
00:46:19.570 --> 00:46:19.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1062
00:46:20.710 --> 00:46:22.250
And this created...
这创造了……

1063
00:46:22.250 --> 00:46:23.410
Fenmel, Fenmel, Flory!
芬梅尔，芬梅尔，弗洛里！

1064
00:46:24.110 --> 00:46:24.870
...number two.
……二把手。

1065
00:46:25.230 --> 00:46:25.590
Oh.
哦。

1066
00:46:25.590 --> 00:46:28.690
A lot of people wrote in.
很多人写信进来了。

1067
00:46:28.970 --> 00:46:29.950
This is a quote.
这是一句引语。

1068
00:46:30.250 --> 00:46:37.250
I am so excited to finally get to discuss my biggest pet peeve in the whole series.
我太兴奋了，终于可以讨论我在整个系列中最看不惯的一件事了。

1069
00:46:37.610 --> 00:46:38.510
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

1070
00:46:39.030 --> 00:46:39.530
What?
什么？

1071
00:46:40.010 --> 00:46:46.830
At 16 minutes, 40 seconds, Jim says he's a great number two for the office.
在16分40秒的时候，吉姆说他是办公室里很棒的二把手。

1072
00:46:47.270 --> 00:46:51.250
And Charles responds by saying he didn't know that position existed.
查尔斯回应说他不知道还有这个职位。

1073
00:46:51.530 --> 00:46:51.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1074
00:46:51.890 --> 00:46:57.370
And then Jim kind of like tap dances and he's like, well, at first it was made up for Dwight,
然后吉姆就开始打圆场，他说，嗯，起初这是为德怀特设立的，

1075
00:46:57.470 --> 00:46:59.390
but then, you know, Michael gave it to me.
但后来，你知道，迈克尔把它给了我。

1076
00:46:59.850 --> 00:47:03.730
And kind of all ends with Charles being like, is this made up position important to you?
最后查尔斯问他，这个虚构的职位对你来说很重要吗？

1077
00:47:03.970 --> 00:47:04.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1078
00:47:05.830 --> 00:47:08.050
Well, people are P.O.ed.
好吧，大家都很生气。

1079
00:47:08.570 --> 00:47:09.090
At who?
生谁的气？

1080
00:47:09.650 --> 00:47:10.490
Here's the thing.
问题是这样的。

1081
00:47:11.110 --> 00:47:18.230
I mean, people sent in lists of evidence to say that this number two position that Jim holds is real.
我是说，人们寄来了证据清单，证明吉姆担任的这个二把手职位是真实存在的。

1082
00:47:18.230 --> 00:47:22.230
It is not a made up position and that Charles should know that.
这不是一个虚构的职位，查尔斯应该知道这一点。

1083
00:47:22.810 --> 00:47:23.950
Here's the evidence.
证据如下。

1084
00:47:24.290 --> 00:47:28.870
In branch closing, Jan is talking to Jim about going back to Scranton.
在《分部关闭》那集，简和吉姆谈论回到斯克兰顿的事。

1085
00:47:28.950 --> 00:47:30.070
And she says, quote,
她说，引用一下，

1086
00:47:30.290 --> 00:47:33.530
We'd like to offer you the number two position at that branch.
我们想给你提供那个分部的二把手职位。

1087
00:47:34.110 --> 00:47:38.390
In the merger, Michael is on the phone with Jan after firing Tony.
在《合并》那集，迈克尔在解雇托尼后和简通电话。

1088
00:47:38.690 --> 00:47:42.470
